# bone — matplotlib's `bone` colormap: the deliberately low-chroma palette.
#
# Derived the same way as cool/winter/spring/summer/autumn/plasma, with one
# departure that matters: the ramp is NOT pastelised toward white. bone is
# already a near-monochrome blue-grey, and blending it toward white collapses
# the five steps into five indistinguishable greys -- measured, at strength
# 0.68 they came out #ADADAD, #BFBFC6, #D1D5DB, #E3EDED, which is not a ramp.
# The values below are bone's own, sampled at t = .24 .40 .58 .78 .94.
#
# This palette exists to fill a measured gap. Across the other seventeen,
# ramp chroma ran 0.15 to 0.66 with nothing deliberately at the bottom; every
# palette was a hue choice. bone is the one that is not -- it is a desktop with
# almost no colour in it at all, which is as different from Catppuccin as a
# light palette is.
#
# THE ALERT ROLES ARE THE EXCEPTION, and deliberately so. A strictly monochrome
# palette cannot signal anything: a critical battery drawn in grey on grey is
# not a warning. URGENT, WARN and GOOD keep just enough chroma to be
# unmistakable and no more, so they read as the only coloured things on screen
# -- which, on this palette, makes them louder than a saturated palette could.

# -- neutrals: bone's dark end ----------------------------------------------
COOL_BG0=#16161E          # t=0.10
COOL_BG1=#232331          # t=0.16
COOL_BG2=#35354A          # t=0.24
COOL_FG0=#EAF2F2          # t=0.94
COOL_FG1=#D6E5E5          # t=0.88
COOL_DIM=#B2CECE          # t=0.78
COOL_DIMMER=#8194A1       # t=0.58
# -- the ramp: bone, unpastelised -------------------------------------------
COOL_0=#35354A
COOL_1=#4C4C6A
COOL_2=#8194A1
COOL_3=#B2CECE
COOL_4=#EAF2F2
# -- alert pair -------------------------------------------------------------
COOL_HOT_0=#98B3B8
COOL_HOT_4=#D6E5E5
# -- off-ramp tints ---------------------------------------------------------
COOL_MINT=#B2CECE
COOL_BLUSH=#D6E5E5
# -- semantic aliases -------------------------------------------------------
COOL_ACCENT=#98B3B8
COOL_ACTIVE=#D6E5E5
COOL_URGENT=#C86A6A       # the only real colour here, and that is the point
COOL_WARN=#C8A46A
COOL_GOOD=#8FB38F
COOL_INACTIVE=#35354A
